  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "UA_Connection_processChunks",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_connection.c",
    "description": "Root cause is missing empty-input validation before pointer arithmetic and dereference in chunk parsing. UA_Connection_processChunks sets `end = &packet->data[packet->length]` and then calls processChunk with `pos = packet->data`. For a zero-length packet where `packet->data` is NULL (as produced by the fuzz harness for input_length=0), this computes an invalid pointer and enters undefined behavior; subsequent parsing can lead to a wild control flow / SEGV in heap memory. The crash may surface away from this frame, but the bug is the unsafe handling of empty/NULL ByteString input in this function/path.",
    "conditions": "Triggered by fuzz_binary_message when the input size is 0. Data flow: LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput allocates a UA_ByteString of size 0 and calls UA_Server_processBinaryMessage -> UA_Connection_processChunks. Because no guard rejects `packet==NULL`, `packet->data==NULL`, or `packet->length==0` before `&packet->data[packet->length]` and chunk processing, the malformed empty packet reaches unsafe pointer operations and causes UBSan deadly signal (wild jump/SEGV)."
  },
